    {
      "body": "I found the root cause. It's a data/config mismatch, not a code bug: cell 11 builds a validation `FlareDSDataset` and it raises because there is **zero overlap** between the validation split's dates and the flare catalog's dates.\n\n- `data.valid_data_path` (`surya_aws_s3_val.csv`) only contains **January** timesteps (across 2011\u20132024).\n- `data.flare_index_path` (`Surya_ML_data_Training_with_intensity.csv`, a 10-row hand-curated catalog with matching mask bitmaps already downloaded in `mask_bitmaps/`) only has events in **April\u2013November 2013**.\n- With `ds_time_tolerance: 4d`, no January Surya timestep is ever within 4 days of any of those 10 events, so the merge_asof intersection is empty \u2014 hence `ValueError: No intersection between Surya and DS indices`.\n- The **train** dataset built fine because `train_data_path` spans full years, including the months the 10 events fall in.\n\nThis is a train/val-splitting design issue for a small, hand-curated catalog: the generic `build_helio_dataloaders` pattern splits by which Surya month-file a timestamp falls in, which works when the downstream catalog is large and spread across the calendar, but with only 10 events concentrated in specific months, reserving \"January\" for validation guarantees zero overlap.",
      "id": "f37f732b-0505-4bf0-95d9-1ea995d7bd86",
      "type": "msg",
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "raw_time": false,
      "mentions": [],
      "time": 1789500558.9755852
    },
    {
      "time": 1789500559.334582,
      "mentions": [],
      "body": "",
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "id": "41874f98-e964-4e84-92c8-1b8e345934b6",
