            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_01GYunXsh2c38UxhbCVBw6HR",
            "raw_input": {
              "question": "How would you like to resolve the validation-split mismatch for this 10-event flare catalog?",
              "options": "[{\"label\": \"Quick unblock\", \"description\": \"Point data.valid_data_path at the same file as train_data_path (config-only change) so the notebook runs end-to-end for exploration. Train and val will draw from the same underlying Surya index/date range, so this is not a real train/val split \u2014 fine for a sanity/dimension check, not for real model selection.\"}, {\"label\": \"Event-level split\", \"description\": \"Add logic so the 10 flare events themselves are split (e.g. 8 train / 2 val) instead of relying on which calendar month a timestamp falls in. Requires a small code change (e.g. a new kwarg/filter in FlareDSDataset or the config) so train/val are genuinely different events.\"}, {\"label\": \"Wait for full catalog\", \"description\": \"Treat this as expected behavior for a placeholder 10-row catalog. No code/config change now \u2014 once you swap in the real, larger flare catalog spanning many months, the existing month-based Surya split should naturally give both train and val overlap.\"}]"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "raw_time": false
    },
    {
      "id": "d9253e22-6572-41a7-ab01-a52048ca948f",
      "time": 1789500573.8735838,
      "mentions": [],
      "body": "AskUserQuestion isn't available in this session, so I'll ask directly: the failure in cell 11 is a data mismatch, not a bug \u2014 the validation split (`surya_aws_s3_val.csv`) only contains January timesteps across 2011\u20132024, while your 10-event flare catalog only has events between April and November 2013. With a 4-day tolerance, there's no way for those to intersect, so `FlareDSDataset` raises when building the val set. The train set works because `train_data_path` spans full years.\n\nHow would you like to resolve it?\n\n1. **Quick unblock** \u2014 point `data.valid_data_path` at the same file as `train_data_path` (config-only) so the notebook runs end-to-end. Train/val would then draw from the same date range, so it's not a real train/val split \u2014 fine for a sanity/dimension check, not for real model selection.\n2. **Event-level split** \u2014 add logic so the 10 flare events themselves get split (e.g. 8 train / 2 val) rather than relying on which calendar month a timestamp falls in. This needs a small code change (e.g. a filter/kwarg in `FlareDSDataset`) so train and val are genuinely different events.\n3. **Wait for the full catalog** \u2014 treat this as expected for a 10-row placeholder; no change now, and once you swap in the real larger catalog spanning many months, the existing month-based split should naturally overlap.\n\nWhich do you want, or something else?",
      "type": "msg",
      "raw_time": false,
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona"
    },
    {
      "metadata": {
        "to_persona": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
        "settings": {
          "__mode__": "plan"
        },
        "model": {
          "settings": {},
          "id": "sonnet"
        }
      },
      "type": "msg",
      "body": "I would choose the event level split",
      "sender": "ahn",
      "id": "2e0b8ea6-b047-43c9-9568-8af929e20085",
      "time": 1789502156.9935567,
      "raw_time": false
    },
    {
      "metadata": {
        "tool_calls": [
          {
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_01LziFLVHzzRzxj1QokbyFed",
            "title": "Read builders.py",
            "kind": "read",
            "raw_output": "1\t\"\"\"\n2\tDataset and DataLoader construction shared by every Surya downstream app.\n3\t\n4\t``HelioNetCDFDataset`` takes ~20 constructor arguments, all of which come straight from\n5\tthe ``data:`` and ``training:`` sections of the config. Spelling that block out at every\n6\tentry point means the same 20 lines get copied into every notebook and every training\n7\tscript, and they drift: one copy forgets ``phase=\"val\"``, another hardcodes a flag the\n8\tYAML was supposed to control.\n9\t\n10\tThese builders own that block once. A downstream app supplies its dataset subclass and\n11\twhatever task-specific keyword arguments that subclass adds::\n12\t\n13\t    train_loader, val_loader = build_helio_dataloaders(\n14\t        cfg,\n15\t        FlareDSDataset,\n16\t        ds_flare_index_path=cfg.data.flare_index_path,\n17\t        label_transform=my_label_transform,\n18\t    )\n19\t\"\"\"\n20\t\n21\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n22\t\n23\timport random\n24\tfrom functools import partial\n25\tfrom typing import Any, Tuple, Type\n26\t\n27\timport numpy as np\n28\timport torch\n29\tfrom torch.utils.data import DataLoader, Dataset\n30\t\n31\tfrom workshop_infrastructure.utils import build_scalers\n32\t\n33\t\n34\tdef _seed_worker(worker_id: int, base_seed: int) -> None:\n35\t    \"\"\"Seed every RNG a DataLoader worker might draw from.\n36\t\n37\t    Seeding torch alone is not enough: ``RandomChannelMaskerTransform`` in\n38\t    ``workshop_infrastructure/datasets/helio.py`` draws from Python's ``random``\n39\t    (``random.sample`` / ``random.random``), and downstream datasets commonly use NumPy.\n40\t\n41\t    Supplying this deliberately displaces Lightning's auto-injected\n42\t    ``pl_worker_init_function``, which derives worker seeds from ``torch.initial_seed()``\n43\t    \u2014 i.e. from the ambient global RNG state, which is exactly the coupling we are\n44\t    removing here.\n45\t    \"\"\"\n46\t    seed = (base_seed + worker_id) % (2 ** 32)\n47\t    random.seed(seed)\n48\t    np.random.seed(seed)\n49\t    torch.manual_seed(seed)\n50\t\n51\t\n52\tdef _base_dataset_kwargs(cfg, scalers) -> dict:\n53\t    \"\"\"Map a TrainingConfig onto the HelioNetCDFDataset constructor arguments.\n54\t\n55\t    This is the single place where config field names meet dataset parameter names.\n56\t    \"\"\"\n57\t    return dict(\n58\t        # Temporal sampling\n59\t        time_delta_input_minutes=cfg.data.time_delta_input_minutes,\n60\t        time_delta_target_minutes=cfg.data.time_delta_target_minutes,\n61\t        n_input_timestamps=cfg.model.time_embedding.time_dim,\n62\t        rollout_steps=cfg.rollout_steps,\n63\t        # Channels and normalization\n64\t        channels=cfg.data.channels,\n65\t        scalers=scalers,\n66\t        # Augmentation\n67\t        drop_hmi_probability=cfg.drop_hmi_probability,\n68\t        use_latitude_in_learned_flow=cfg.use_latitude_in_learned_flow,\n69\t        # Storage: local root, and how s3:// paths in the index are read\n70\t        sdo_data_root_path=cfg.data.sdo_data_root_path,\n71\t        s3_mode=cfg.data.s3_mode,\n72\t        s3_storage_options={\"anon\": cfg.data.s3_anon},\n73\t        s3_cache_dir=cfg.data.s3_cache_dir,\n74\t        s3_boto3_max_concurrency=cfg.data.s3_boto3_max_concurrency,\n75\t        s3_boto3_part_size_mb=cfg.data.s3_boto3_part_size_mb,\n76\t    )\n77\t\n78\t\n79\tdef build_helio_datasets(\n80\t    cfg,\n81\t    dataset_cls: Type[Dataset],\n82\t    scalers: Any = None,\n83\t    **task_kwargs,\n84\t) -> Tuple[Dataset, Dataset]:\n85\t    \"\"\"Build the train and validation datasets described by ``cfg``.\n86\t\n87\t    Args:\n88\t        cfg: A ``TrainingConfig`` from ``load_config()``.\n89\t        dataset_cls: ``HelioNetCDFDataset`` or a subclass of it.\n90\t        scalers: Normalization statistics. Built from ``cfg.data.scalers_path`` if omitted;\n91\t            pass an existing dict to avoid re-reading the YAML.\n92\t        **task_kwargs: Extra keyword arguments forwarded to ``dataset_cls`` \u2014 the\n93\t            task-specific parameters your subclass adds.\n94\t\n95\t    Returns:\n96\t        ``(train_dataset, val_dataset)``. They differ only in the index they read and in\n97\t        ``phase``: the validation set uses ``phase=\"val\"``, which disables the random\n98\t        channel masking and vertical flips that are applied during training.\n99\t    \"\"\"\n100\t    if scalers is None:\n101\t        scalers = build_scalers(info=cfg.data.scalers_path)\n102\t\n103\t    common = {**_base_dataset_kwargs(cfg, scalers), **task_kwargs}\n104\t\n105\t    train_dataset = dataset_cls(index_path=cfg.data.train_data_path, phase=\"train\", **common)\n106\t    val_dataset = dataset_cls(index_path=cfg.data.valid_data_path, phase=\"val\", **common)\n107\t    return train_dataset, val_dataset\n108\t\n109\t\n110\tdef build_helio_dataloaders(\n111\t    cfg,\n112\t    dataset_cls: Type[Dataset],\n113\t    scalers: Any = None,\n114\t    num_workers: int | None = None,\n115\t    seed: int | None = None,\n116\t    **task_kwargs,\n117\t) -> Tuple[DataLoader, DataLoader]:\n118\t    \"\"\"Build the train and validation DataLoaders described by ``cfg``.\n119\t\n120\t    Args:\n121\t        cfg: A ``TrainingConfig`` from ``load_config()``.\n122\t        dataset_cls: ``HelioNetCDFDataset`` or a subclass of it.\n123\t        scalers: Normalization statistics; built from the config if omitted.\n124\t        num_workers: Override for ``cfg.num_workers`` (useful in notebooks, where fewer\n125\t            workers start faster).\n126\t        seed: Seed for the shuffle order and the per-worker RNGs. Defaults to ``cfg.seed``.\n127\t            Pinning it explicitly is what makes the epoch order depend only on the config:\n128\t            a bare ``shuffle=True`` seeds its sampler from whatever the global torch RNG\n129\t            state happens to be when the iterator is created, so anything that consumes\n130\t            RNG earlier in the program silently reshuffles the data.\n131\t        **task_kwargs: Extra keyword arguments forwarded to ``dataset_cls``.\n132\t\n133\t    Returns:\n134\t        ``(train_loader, val_loader)``. Only the training loader shuffles.\n135\t    \"\"\"\n136\t    train_dataset, val_dataset = build_helio_datasets(\n137\t        cfg, dataset_cls, scalers=scalers, **task_kwargs\n138\t    )\n139\t\n140\t    workers = cfg.num_workers if num_workers is None else num_workers\n141\t    base_seed = cfg.seed if seed is None else seed\n142\t\n143\t    loader_kwargs = dict(\n144\t        batch_size=cfg.batch_size,\n145\t        num_workers=workers,\n146\t        pin_memory=True,\n147\t        drop_last=True,\n148\t    )\n149\t    if workers > 0:\n150\t        # \"spawn\": the dataset holds an s3fs/boto3 handle that does not survive fork.\n151\t        # Both of these are rejected outright when num_workers == 0.\n152\t        loader_kwargs[\"multiprocessing_context\"] = \"spawn\"\n153\t        loader_kwargs[\"persistent_workers\"] = True\n154\t        loader_kwargs[\"worker_init_fn\"] = partial(_seed_worker, base_seed=base_seed)\n155\t\n156\t    # An explicit generator makes the shuffle a function of the seed alone, rather than\n157\t    # of the global RNG state at the moment the iterator happens to be created.\n158\t    shuffle_generator = torch.Generator()\n159\t    shuffle_generator.manual_seed(base_seed)\n160\t\n161\t    train_loader = DataLoader(\n162\t        train_dataset, shuffle=True, generator=shuffle_generator, **loader_kwargs\n163\t    )\n164\t    # No generator for validation: it is not shuffled, so there is nothing to seed.\n165\t    val_loader = DataLoader(val_dataset, shuffle=False, **loader_kwargs)\n166\t    return train_loader, val_loader\n167\t",
            "locations": [
              "/home/jovyan/adi_wdir/surya_workshop/workshop_infrastructure/datasets/builders.py"
            ],
