          {
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_017QH5fMqKs7PkYqMG4X7vJu",
            "title": "Read configs.py (1 - 60)",
            "status": "completed",
            "raw_output": "1\t\"\"\"\n2\tTyped configuration for Surya downstream applications.\n3\t\n4\tEverything a fine-tuning run needs is declared here:\n5\t\n6\t- ``TimeEmbeddingConfig`` / ``LoraAdapterConfig`` / ``ModelConfig`` \u2014 the backbone\n7\t  architecture and fine-tuning head, mirroring the HelioSpectformer constructors.\n8\t- ``DataConfig`` / ``OutputConfig`` / ``TrainingConfig`` \u2014 the parts of a run that every\n9\t  downstream task has: what data to load, where checkpoints go, and the optimizer /\n10\t  logging settings.\n11\t- ``load_config()`` \u2014 the single entry point. Reads the YAML and returns a fully typed\n12\t  ``TrainingConfig``, so downstream code never passes raw dicts around.\n13\t\n14\t**Adding task-specific settings:** subclass ``DataConfig`` in your app and pass the\n15\tsubclass to ``load_config(path, data_cls=YourDataConfig)``. You do not copy this file.\n16\tSee ``downstream_apps/template/configs.py`` for a worked example.\n17\t\"\"\"\n18\t\n19\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n20\t\n21\timport os\n22\tfrom dataclasses import MISSING, dataclass, field, fields as dc_fields\n23\tfrom pathlib import Path\n24\tfrom typing import ClassVar, List, Optional, Union\n25\t\n26\timport yaml\n27\t\n28\t# Environment variable consulted when data.s3_cache_dir is left unset in the config.\n29\t# It lets one committed config run on machines with different scratch space, without an\n30\t# absolute path pointing into one user's home ending up in version control.\n31\tS3_CACHE_DIR_ENV_VAR = \"SURYA_WS_CACHE_DIR\"\n32\t\n33\t\n34\t# How HelioNetCDFDataset reads s3:// paths. Declared here rather than in helio.py so the\n35\t# config layer can reject a bad value at startup, before any dataset is constructed.\n36\t#   \"download\"    \u2014 fetch the whole object into s3_cache_dir, then open it locally.\n37\t#                   Recommended: NetCDF/HDF5 needs random seeks that streaming cannot serve.\n38\t#   \"simplecache\" \u2014 fsspec read-through cache into s3_cache_dir.\n39\t#   \"stream\"      \u2014 direct s3fs handle, no local cache. Works, but roughly 9x slower on\n40\t#                   full SDO frames: HDF5 random access becomes many small ranged GETs.\n41\tVALID_S3_MODES = (\"download\", \"simplecache\", \"stream\")\n42\t\n43\t# Accepted values for training.deterministic, passed straight to lightning.Trainer.\n44\t#   False   \u2014 no determinism guarantees; two identical runs may differ. The default,\n45\t#             chosen for throughput: determinism costs roughly 20% of wall time.\n46\t#   \"warn\"  \u2014 bit-identical wherever a deterministic kernel exists; warn (naming the op)\n47\t#             where one does not. Never blocks a run. Switch to this whenever you need to\n48\t#             attribute a change in results to your edit rather than to run-to-run drift.\n49\t#   True    \u2014 hard guarantee; any op without a deterministic kernel raises. Note that\n50\t#             model.learned_flow uses F.grid_sample, which has no deterministic CUDA\n51\t#             backward, so learned_flow: true is incompatible with this setting.\n52\tVALID_DETERMINISTIC = (True, False, \"warn\")\n53\t\n54\t\n55\t@dataclass\n56\tclass TimeEmbeddingConfig:\n57\t    \"\"\"Controls how temporal position is encoded before the transformer blocks.\"\"\"\n58\t    type: str = \"linear\"         # \"linear\" | \"fourier\" | \"perceiver\"\n59\t    n_queries: Optional[int] = None  # Required for \"perceiver\"; unused otherwise\n60\t    time_dim: int = 1            # Number of input timesteps",
            "kind": "read",
