            "kind": "edit",
            "raw_input": {
              "file_path": "/home/jovyan/.claude/plans/adi-wdir-surya-workshop-downstream-apps-partitioned-wand.md",
              "content": "# Fix validation-split mismatch in sf_triggers via event-level split\n\n## Context\n\n`1_baseline_template.ipynb` cell `70e9c5b2` fails with `ValueError: No intersection between\nSurya and DS indices` when `build_helio_dataloaders()` constructs the **validation**\n`FlareDSDataset`.\n\nRoot cause (confirmed by inspecting the data directly, not a code bug):\n- `data.valid_data_path` (`surya_aws_s3_val.csv`) contains only **January** Surya timesteps\n  (across 2011\u20132024).\n- `data.flare_index_path` (`/home/jovyan/scratch_space/adithya_hn/Surya_ML_data_Training_with_intensity.csv`)\n  is a hand-curated, 10-event catalog, all falling between **April and November 2013** \u2014\n  chosen because `mask_dir` only has SHARP bitmap masks downloaded for exactly those 10 events.\n- With `ds_time_tolerance: 4d`, no January Surya timestep is ever close enough to any of the\n  10 events, so the merge in `FlareDSDataset.__init__` (`downstream_apps/sf_triggers/datasets/sf_triggers_dataset.py:104-131`)\n  drops every row and raises. Training works today only because `train_data_path` spans full\n  years and happens to include Apr\u2013Nov.\n\nThe user chose the **event-level split** fix: instead of relying on which calendar-month Surya\nfile a timestamp lands in (meaningless with only 10 concentrated events), split the 10 flare\n*events themselves* into train/val subsets, and match both subsets against the same full-year\nSurya index.\n\n## Changes\n\n### 1. `downstream_apps/sf_triggers/datasets/sf_triggers_dataset.py`\n\nIn `FlareDSDataset.__init__`:\n- Add two new keyword args: `ds_val_fraction: float = 0.2`, `ds_split_seed: int = 42`.\n- Immediately after `self.ds_index.sort_values(\"ds_index\", inplace=True)` (currently line 101)\n  and before building `self.df_valid_indices`, deterministically split `self.ds_index` by\n  event using `self.phase` (already set by `super().__init__()` at this point):\n\n  ```python\n  n_events = len(self.ds_index)\n  rng = np.random.RandomState(ds_split_seed)\n  shuffled = rng.permutation(n_events)\n  n_val = max(1, round(n_events * ds_val_fraction))\n  val_positions = set(shuffled[:n_val])\n  positions = val_positions if self.phase == \"val\" else set(range(n_events)) - val_positions\n  self.ds_index = self.ds_index.iloc[sorted(positions)]\n  ```\n\n  This is deterministic and seed-driven, so the train dataset and val dataset \u2014 built as two\n  separate `FlareDSDataset` instances \u2014 agree on a disjoint partition without communicating.\n- Update the class docstring's \"Additional Args\" section to document the two new parameters.\n\n### 2. `downstream_apps/sf_triggers/configs.py`\n\nAdd two plain (non-path) fields to `FlareDataConfig`, following the existing style of\n`ds_time_tolerance` / `ds_match_direction`:\n```python\nds_val_fraction: float = 0.2\nds_split_seed: int = 42\n```\n\n### 3. `downstream_apps/sf_triggers/configs/config_script.yaml`\n\n- Point `valid_data_path` at the same file as `train_data_path`\n  (`../../../data/indices/surya_aws_s3_train.csv`), with a comment explaining why: this app's\n  train/val split happens at the flare-*event* level inside `FlareDSDataset`, not by which\n  Surya calendar-month file a timestep falls in \u2014 the arbitrary January-only reserved window\n  never overlaps a small, calendar-concentrated event catalog like this one.\n- Add `ds_val_fraction: 0.2` and `ds_split_seed: 42` under the \"Downstream label alignment\"\n  block, matching the existing explicit-value style of the file.\n\n### 4. `1_baseline_template.ipynb`, cell `70e9c5b2`\n\nAdd the two new kwargs to the `build_helio_dataloaders(...)` call, alongside the existing\n`ds_time_tolerance=cfg.data.ds_time_tolerance` etc.:\n```python\nds_val_fraction=cfg.data.ds_val_fraction,\nds_split_seed=cfg.data.ds_split_seed,\n```\n\nNot touched: `3_finetune_template_1D.py` in this app still imports from\n`downstream_apps.template` (a stale leftover from scaffolding, unrelated to\n`sf_triggers_dataset.py`) \u2014 out of scope for this fix.\n\n## Verification\n\n1. Re-run the notebook via the Jupyter MCP tools from cell `63c1fe60` (config load) through\n   `70e9c5b2` (or `run_all_cells`), confirm no `ValueError` is raised.\n2. Print `train_data_loader.dataset.df_valid_indices[\"ds_index\"]` and the same for\n   `val_data_loader.dataset` \u2014 confirm the two event-timestamp sets are disjoint (8 vs 2 events)\n   and both non-empty.\n3. Confirm `len(train_data_loader.dataset)` and `len(val_data_loader.dataset)` are both > 0\n   and print as before.\n4. Continue past cell 11 (batch inspection, model forward, metrics cells) to confirm nothing\n   downstream broke.\n"
            },
            "diffs": [
              {
                "path": "/home/jovyan/.claude/plans/adi-wdir-surya-workshop-downstream-apps-partitioned-wand.md",
                "new_text": "# Fix validation-split mismatch in sf_triggers via event-level split\n\n## Context\n\n`1_baseline_template.ipynb` cell `70e9c5b2` fails with `ValueError: No intersection between\nSurya and DS indices` when `build_helio_dataloaders()` constructs the **validation**\n`FlareDSDataset`.\n\nRoot cause (confirmed by inspecting the data directly, not a code bug):\n- `data.valid_data_path` (`surya_aws_s3_val.csv`) contains only **January** Surya timesteps\n  (across 2011\u20132024).\n- `data.flare_index_path` (`/home/jovyan/scratch_space/adithya_hn/Surya_ML_data_Training_with_intensity.csv`)\n  is a hand-curated, 10-event catalog, all falling between **April and November 2013** \u2014\n  chosen because `mask_dir` only has SHARP bitmap masks downloaded for exactly those 10 events.\n- With `ds_time_tolerance: 4d`, no January Surya timestep is ever close enough to any of the\n  10 events, so the merge in `FlareDSDataset.__init__` (`downstream_apps/sf_triggers/datasets/sf_triggers_dataset.py:104-131`)\n  drops every row and raises. Training works today only because `train_data_path` spans full\n  years and happens to include Apr\u2013Nov.\n\nThe user chose the **event-level split** fix: instead of relying on which calendar-month Surya\nfile a timestamp lands in (meaningless with only 10 concentrated events), split the 10 flare\n*events themselves* into train/val subsets, and match both subsets against the same full-year\nSurya index.\n\n## Changes\n\n### 1. `downstream_apps/sf_triggers/datasets/sf_triggers_dataset.py`\n\nIn `FlareDSDataset.__init__`:\n- Add two new keyword args: `ds_val_fraction: float = 0.2`, `ds_split_seed: int = 42`.\n- Immediately after `self.ds_index.sort_values(\"ds_index\", inplace=True)` (currently line 101)\n  and before building `self.df_valid_indices`, deterministically split `self.ds_index` by\n  event using `self.phase` (already set by `super().__init__()` at this point):\n\n  ```python\n  n_events = len(self.ds_index)\n  rng = np.random.RandomState(ds_split_seed)\n  shuffled = rng.permutation(n_events)\n  n_val = max(1, round(n_events * ds_val_fraction))\n  val_positions = set(shuffled[:n_val])\n  positions = val_positions if self.phase == \"val\" else set(range(n_events)) - val_positions\n  self.ds_index = self.ds_index.iloc[sorted(positions)]\n  ```\n\n  This is deterministic and seed-driven, so the train dataset and val dataset \u2014 built as two\n  separate `FlareDSDataset` instances \u2014 agree on a disjoint partition without communicating.\n- Update the class docstring's \"Additional Args\" section to document the two new parameters.\n\n### 2. `downstream_apps/sf_triggers/configs.py`\n\nAdd two plain (non-path) fields to `FlareDataConfig`, following the existing style of\n`ds_time_tolerance` / `ds_match_direction`:\n```python\nds_val_fraction: float = 0.2\nds_split_seed: int = 42\n```\n\n### 3. `downstream_apps/sf_triggers/configs/config_script.yaml`\n\n- Point `valid_data_path` at the same file as `train_data_path`\n  (`../../../data/indices/surya_aws_s3_train.csv`), with a comment explaining why: this app's\n  train/val split happens at the flare-*event* level inside `FlareDSDataset`, not by which\n  Surya calendar-month file a timestep falls in \u2014 the arbitrary January-only reserved window\n  never overlaps a small, calendar-concentrated event catalog like this one.\n- Add `ds_val_fraction: 0.2` and `ds_split_seed: 42` under the \"Downstream label alignment\"\n  block, matching the existing explicit-value style of the file.\n\n### 4. `1_baseline_template.ipynb`, cell `70e9c5b2`\n\nAdd the two new kwargs to the `build_helio_dataloaders(...)` call, alongside the existing\n`ds_time_tolerance=cfg.data.ds_time_tolerance` etc.:\n```python\nds_val_fraction=cfg.data.ds_val_fraction,\nds_split_seed=cfg.data.ds_split_seed,\n```\n\nNot touched: `3_finetune_template_1D.py` in this app still imports from\n`downstream_apps.template` (a stale leftover from scaffolding, unrelated to\n`sf_triggers_dataset.py`) \u2014 out of scope for this fix.\n\n## Verification\n\n1. Re-run the notebook via the Jupyter MCP tools from cell `63c1fe60` (config load) through\n   `70e9c5b2` (or `run_all_cells`), confirm no `ValueError` is raised.\n2. Print `train_data_loader.dataset.df_valid_indices[\"ds_index\"]` and the same for\n   `val_data_loader.dataset` \u2014 confirm the two event-timestamp sets are disjoint (8 vs 2 events)\n   and both non-empty.\n3. Confirm `len(train_data_loader.dataset)` and `len(val_data_loader.dataset)` are both > 0\n   and print as before.\n4. Continue past cell 11 (batch inspection, model forward, metrics cells) to confirm nothing\n   downstream broke.\n"
              }
            ]
