ter `self.ds_index.sort_values(\"ds_index\", inplace=True)` (currently line 101)\n  and before building `self.df_valid_indices`, deterministically split `self.ds_index` by\n  event using `self.phase` (already set by `super().__init__()` at this point):\n\n  ```python\n  n_events = len(self.ds_index)\n  rng = np.random.RandomState(ds_split_seed)\n  shuffled = rng.permutation(n_events)\n  n_val = max(1, round(n_events * ds_val_fraction))\n  val_positions = set(shuffled[:n_val])\n  positions = val_positions if self.phase == \"val\" else set(range(n_events)) - val_positions\n  self.ds_index = self.ds_index.iloc[sorted(positions)]\n  ```\n\n  This is deterministic and seed-driven, so the train dataset and val dataset \u2014 built as two\n  separate `FlareDSDataset` instances \u2014 agree on a disjoint partition without communicating.\n- Update the class docstring's \"Additional Args\" section to document the two new parameters.\n\n### 2. `downstream_apps/sf_triggers/configs.py`\n\nAdd two plain (non-path) fields to `FlareDataConfig`, following the existing style of\n`ds_time_tolerance` / `ds_match_direction`:\n```python\nds_val_fraction: float = 0.2\nds_split_seed: int = 42\n```\n\n### 3. `downstream_apps/sf_triggers/configs/config_script.yaml`\n\n- Point `valid_data_path` at the same file as `train_data_path`\n  (`../../../data/indices/surya_aws_s3_train.csv`), with a comment explaining why: this app's\n  train/val split happens at the flare-*event* level inside `FlareDSDataset`, not by which\n  Surya calendar-month file a timestep falls in \u2014 the arbitrary January-only reserved window\n  never overlaps a small, calendar-concentrated event catalog like this one.\n- Add `ds_val_fraction: 0.2` and `ds_split_seed: 42` under the \"Downstream label alignment\"\n  block, matching the existing explicit-value style of the file.\n\n### 4. `1_baseline_template.ipynb`, cell `70e9c5b2`\n\nAdd the two new kwargs to the `build_helio_dataloaders(...)` call, alongside the existing\