_triggers_dataset.py`) \u2014 out of scope for this fix.\n\n## Verification\n\n1. Re-run the notebook via the Jupyter MCP tools from cell `63c1fe60` (config load) through\n   `70e9c5b2` (or `run_all_cells`), confirm no `ValueError` is raised.\n2. Print `train_data_loader.dataset.df_valid_indices[\"ds_index\"]` and the same for\n   `val_data_loader.dataset` \u2014 confirm the two event-timestamp sets are disjoint (8 vs 2 events)\n   and both non-empty.\n3. Confirm `len(train_data_loader.dataset)` and `len(val_data_loader.dataset)` are both > 0\n   and print as before.\n4. Continue past cell 11 (batch inspection, model forward, metrics cells) to confirm nothing\n   downstream broke.\n",
